'''''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]''''' returned for its '''twelfth series''' beginning from 7 September 2014 with a launch show,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b04hg33y|title=BBC One – Strictly Come Dancing, Series 12, The Launch Show|publisher=BBC}}</ref> and the live shows began on 26 and 27 September.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/showsandtours/shows/strictly_come_dancing_2014|title=BBC – Be in the audience – Strictly Come Dancing|publisher=BBC|access-date=5 October 2014|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140823224813/http://www.bbc.co.uk/showsandtours/shows/strictly_come_dancing_2014|archive-date=23 August 2014}}</ref>

After [[Sir Bruce Forsyth]] announced his departure from the show at the end of the [[Strictly Come Dancing series 11|previous series]] (He would continue to host the [[Strictly Come Dancing Christmas Specials|Christmas]] and [[Children in Need]] specials)<ref name="digitalspy">{{cite web |date=4 April 2014 |title=Strictly Come Dancing: Sir Bruce Forsyth steps down from live shows – Strictly Come Dancing News – Reality TV |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a562475/strictly-come-dancing-sir-bruce-forsyth-steps-down-from-live-shows.html#~oFWGhgDgukrCSF |accessdate=1 June 2014 |work=Digital Spy}}</ref> [[Tess Daly]] returned to present the main show on [[BBC One]] alongside [[Claudia Winkleman]], who was promoted to co-presenter in addition to the results show, this change would last for 12 additional series until 2025.<ref name="digitalspy2">{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a569987/claudia-winkleman-tess-daly-confirmed-as-strictly-come-dancing-hosts.html#~oFWDOlsF63gXTt|title=Claudia Winkleman, Tess Daly confirmed as Strictly Come Dancing hosts – Strictly Come Dancing News – Reality TV|work=Digital Spy|date=9 May 2014|accessdate=1 June 2014}}</ref> [[Zoe Ball]] returned as presenter of the spin-off show ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]]'' on [[BBC Two]]. Judges [[Darcey Bussell]], [[Len Goodman]], [[Craig Revel Horwood]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] also returned.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://tellymix.co.uk/reality-tv/strictly-come-dancing/187612-all-four-strictly-come-dancing-judges-to-return-for-2014-series.html |title=All four Strictly Come Dancing judges to return for 2014 series |publisher=Tellymix |date=27 June 2014 |accessdate=14 July 2014}}</ref>

The shows from 1 to 16 November were hosted by Daly and [[Zoe Ball]], after one of Winkleman's children was involved in an accident.<ref name="Winkleman Ball">{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/posts/Zoe-Ball-steps-in-for-Claudia-in-tonights-show|title=BBC – Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Zoe Ball steps in for Claudia in tonight's show|date=November 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a609568/zoe-ball-to-co-present-strictly-come-dancing-this-weekend-from-blackpool.html|title=Zoe Ball to co-present Strictly Come Dancing this weekend from Blackpool|work=Digital Spy|date=12 November 2014}}</ref> Winkleman returned to co-host the show on 22 November.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/posts/Claudia-Winkleman-returns-to-the-Strictly-Ballroom|title=BBC – Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Claudia Winkleman returns to the Strictly Ballroom|date=21 November 2014}}</ref>

[[Caroline Flack]] and [[Pasha Kovalev]] were announced as the winners on 20 December,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/posts/Caroline-Flack-wins-Strictly |title=BBC Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Caroline Flack wins Strictly |date=20 December 2014 |publisher=BBC |accessdate=29 January 2015}}</ref> while [[Simon Webbe]] and [[Kristina Rihanoff]], and [[Frankie Bridge]] and [[Kevin Clifton]] were the runners-up.

