The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. The couples are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the lowest scored couple receiving one point, and the highest scored couple receiving the most points (the maximum number of points available depends on the number of couples remaining in the competition). The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; the couple with the fewest votes receiving one point, and the couple with the most votes receiving the most points.

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence. As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave, with [[Len Goodman]], as head judge, having the last and [[Casting vote|deciding vote]].

== Professional dancers ==
On 1 June 2014, it was revealed that [[Artem Chigvintsev]], [[Anya Garnis]], and [[James Jordan (dancer)|James Jordan]] would not return as professionals,<ref name="digitalspy3">{{cite web |date=June 2014 |title=Strictly Come Dancing: Artem Chigvintsev, James Jordan not returning – Strictly Come Dancing News – Reality TV |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a574743/strictly-come-dancing-artem-chigvintsev-james-jordan-not-returning.html#~oFWzkhJdBKLenl |accessdate=1 June 2014 |work=Digital Spy}}</ref> but that Garnis would still be part of the choreography team. They were replaced by two new professionals, [[Joanne Clifton]] and [[Tristan MacManus]], as well as [[Natalie Lowe]], who returned after missing the last series due to a foot injury.<ref name="bbc">{{cite web |date=June 2014 |title=BBC – Blogs – Strictly Come Dancing – Strictly Come Dancing 2014 Professional Dancers Confirmed |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/posts/Strictly-Come-Dancing-2014-Professional-Dancers-Confirmed |accessdate=28 June 2014 |publisher=BBC}}</ref> On 6 August, it was announced that [[Robin Windsor]] would not be competing as a professional in the series as previously announced due to a back injury; he was replaced by [[Trent Whiddon]].<ref>{{cite web |date=6 August 2014 |title=Strictly Come Dancing 2014: Robin Windsor pulls out of series after suffering back injury – Metro News |url=http://metro.co.uk/2014/08/06/robin-windsor-pulls-out-of-strictly-come-dancing-after-suffering-back-injury-4822029/ |accessdate=5 October 2014 |work=Metro}}</ref>

==Couples==
This series featured fifteen celebrity contestants. [[Frankie Bridge]] was the first contestant announced on 13 August,<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-28769494|title=Strictly Come Dancing: The Saturdays' Frankie Bridge signs up|work=BBC News|date=13 August 2014|accessdate=5 October 2014}}</ref> and additional celebrities were announced throughout the month. The full line-up was revealed by the BBC on 29 August.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-28980260|title=Strictly Come Dancing: Full celebrity line-up confirmed|work=BBC News|date=29 August 2014|accessdate=5 October 2014}}</ref>
